# pyro_activate

- Label: Pyro Activate
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 1 to 3
- Parameters: 22 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/pyro_activate.html
- Summary (EN): The Pyro Activate node changes the activation of VDBs in a Pyro simulation. It turns voxel leaves on or off so the solver runs only where needed, while keeping enough surrounding air for the simulation.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud Pyro Activate active ou désactive les feuilles de voxels d'une simulation Pyro, pour ne résoudre que là où c'est nécessaire ; la page ne couvre pas la version 2.0.

- Inputs meaning: ["density: float VDB, the activation reference that also culls inactive leaves", "temperature: float VDB, used like density", "v: vector VDB supplying velocities for velocity dilation", "flame: float VDB, used like density", "activate_pts: points; any leaf containing a point is activated"]

- Key parameters: ["References: fields that determine activation", "Density Cutoff: leaves whose maximum combined reference value falls below it can be deactivated", "Leaf Dilation / Leaf Dilation Dist: expand the active region by leaves or by world distance (rounded up to the leaf); the larger of the two is used", "Velocity Dilation: expands each leaf by its maximum velocity; related Velocity Scale, Tangential Scale and Ambient Velocity are not explained on the page", "Clip Min/Max X, Y, Z: deactivate leaves outside world-space bounds"]

- Caveats: ["COP Pyro requires DOP-level permissions; it is not in Houdini Core, only in FX, Apprentice, Indie and Education.", "Keep the simulated volume active with a buffer, or the surrounding air field may be missing.", "Leaves are 8x8x8 voxel blocks; fewer active leaves means less memory use and a faster simulation.", "The page covers the base node available since 21.0 and does not cover version 2.0."]

